## Objective

Introduce a transport-agnostic dead message handling abstraction responsible for processing messages that permanently fail after exhausting all configured retry attempts.

This task completes the retry pipeline while intentionally remaining independent of Kafka, DLQs, or persistent storage.

## Context

The retry infrastructure now consists of:

RetryPolicy
BackoffStrategy
RetryScheduler

When the retry policy decides to stop retrying, the dispatcher currently propagates the failure directly.

Instead, permanent failures should be delegated to a dedicated component.

## Scope
In Scope

Create:

platform
└── messaging
    └── retry
        ├── DeadMessageHandler
        ├── LoggingDeadMessageHandler
        └── DeadMessageContext

Example API:

public interface DeadMessageHandler {

    CompletionStage<Void> handle(
        DeadMessageContext context
    );

}

DeadMessageContext should contain the information required to diagnose the failure, for example:

Outbox message
Attempt count
Failure cause
Timestamp

The default implementation (LoggingDeadMessageHandler) should:

log the permanent failure
include retry count
include root exception
complete successfully without throwing

## Dispatcher Integration

When RetryPolicy returns STOP:

Dispatch Failure
        │
        ▼
RetryPolicy
        │
        ├── RETRY ──► Scheduler
        │
        └── STOP
                │
                ▼
DeadMessageHandler

The dispatcher should delegate to DeadMessageHandler before completing the failed dispatch.

## Out of Scope

